      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niantic%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1825, Joseph Strickling, a native of Ohio, erected Niantic's first log cabin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niantic%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village's first schoolhouse, a log cabin, was constructed in 1847 for the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niantic%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1838, the Potawatomi Death Trail cut through Niantic during a tragic migration.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niantic%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Niantic lies 12 miles west of Decatur and 30 miles east‑northeast of Springfield.",
